; Play a sweeping pulse sound
;
; Makes E = A passes. In each pass, N (A counting down from its start value
; to 1) selects one of E port writes (the one where B = N): that write has the
; speaker and MIC bits set, all the others have them clear. The single pulse
; therefore moves one step along the pass each time, which makes a sweeping
; chirp. The other bits written are those of N, so the border colour (bits
; 0-2) also changes from pass to pass.
; .
; #R$88AE calls this after each step of the message that scrolls along the
; bottom of the title screen, with A = (message offset AND $1F) + $32, so the
; sound depends on the position in the message. Observed: with no key pressed
; after the code entry, the title tune ends at about frame 1583 and the first
; call follows with A = $32. Not executed in the coverage maps in re/maps.
; .
; Hardware: writes port $FE (border, speaker, MIC); timing loops.
;
; A Start value of N (about 50 to 81 as called)
; O:A 0
@label=PlaySweepSound
c$96DE LD E,A        ;
@isub=LD C,ULA_PORT
 $96DF LD C,$FE      ;
@label=PlaySweepSound_Pass
*$96E1 LD D,A        ;
 $96E2 RES 4,D       ;
 $96E4 RES 3,D       ;
 $96E6 LD B,E        ;
@label=PlaySweepSound_Step
*$96E7 CP B          ;
 $96E8 JR NZ,$96EC   ;
@isub=LD D,BEEPER_BITS
 $96EA LD D,$18      ;
*$96EC OUT (C),D     ;
 $96EE DJNZ $96E7    ;
 $96F0 DEC A         ;
 $96F1 JR NZ,$96E1   ;
 $96F3 RET           ;
